<SiteLayout title="Halowin Bubo" description="Halowin Bubo is a fork of gufo, ported to native Windows with AMD HIP. See measured speeds, test conditions, and documentation.">
  <span class="eyebrow">Native Windows · AMD HIP</span>
  <h1>Halowin Bubo</h1>
  <p class="intro">Halowin Bubo is a fork of the open-source gufo LLM server. It runs on native Windows with AMD HIP. It is tuned for AMD Strix Halo laptops at about 70 W and for Windows users in general.</p>
  <div class="credit intro">Bubo is built on <a href="https://github.com/gufo-org/gufo">gufo</a>. Credit goes to the gufo authors for the upstream server. gufo uses the MIT license.</div>
  <div class="article-grid">
    <div class="article-body">
      <section aria-labelledby="for"><h2 id="for">For your Windows laptop</h2><p><strong>Supported hardware:</strong> Bubo is built and tested for AMD Strix Halo with 128 GB of memory on Windows, mainly laptops. It can work on other machines, but we make no promise.</p><p>Bubo is tuned for Ryzen AI Max laptops with Radeon 8060S graphics. Use Qwen3.8 Flash Next in GGUF format with the UD-Q4_K_XL quant. Use Performance mode at about 70 W.</p><p><a href="/docs/system-setup/">Set up your system</a> before you install Bubo.</p></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="speed">
        <h2 id="speed">Measured speed</h2>
        <p>Halowin Bubo on the ASUS ProArt PX13 with Radeon 8060S. Windows 11, Performance mode, about 70 W. Qwen3.8 Flash Next UD-Q4_K_XL with an MTP draft head. Tests: 8–10 October 2026.</p>
        <Measurements />
        <p class="benchmark-comparison">With several users at once, Halowin Bubo with MTP reaches 37.4 tok/s for 1 user, 79.2 for 4 users and about 100–107 for 8 users (combined decode, 4K context each, about 70 W). It is ahead of upstream gufo’s published 1-user MTP rate and level with it at 4 users. At 8 users it runs at about 70 W against upstream’s full-power hardware. <a href="/docs/benchmarks/#many-users">See the table</a>.</p>
        <p class="benchmark-comparison">At 140 W, Halowin Bubo is estimated at 1,617–1,762 tok/s prefill (pp2048), level with upstream’s published rate. Upstream gufo publishes 1,700 tok/s on full-power Strix Halo hardware.</p>
        <p class="benchmark-comparison">Reasoning check against stock gufo on 35 GPQA, AIME, HMMT and IMO requests: 29/35 correct for Halowin Bubo and 27/35 for stock gufo, with about 24 % faster decode. Same or better accuracy; the sets are small. <a href="/docs/benchmarks/">See the table</a>.</p>
        <a href="/docs/benchmarks/">Read the benchmark details</a>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="models"><h2 id="models">Supported models</h2><p>Bubo keeps all model families of gufo: DeepSeek V4 Flash, Qwen3.8 27B, Qwen3.8 Flash-Next, Qwen3.6 35B-A3B, Qwen3-ASR 1.7B, Qwen3-TTS 1.7B, Qwen-Image-2.1, and MiniMax H3.</p><p>Bubo is tuned for Qwen3.8 Flash Next. The other models run with upstream gufo settings.</p><a href="/docs/models/">See the model table</a></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="downloads"><h2 id="downloads">Downloads</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/haloforge-labs/bubo/releases/tag/v0.1.0">Halowin Bubo v0.1.0 for Windows (zip and SHA-256) on GitHub</a></p></section>
    </div>
    <aside class="margin-note" aria-label="Halowin Bubo notes">
      <span class="eyebrow">The name</span>
      <h2>An owl genus</h2><p>Bubo is a genus of owl. “Gufo” is Italian for owl.</p>
      <h2>Documentation</h2><p><a href="/docs/">Read the Halowin Bubo docs</a> for system settings, profiles, and known issues.</p>
    </aside>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
